error_log
*ods
*xlsx
log/

# Lock records are runtime state, like log/. The directory and its .htaccess are tracked;
# the records themselves are not.
lpn-locks/*.json

# The browser pass installs playwright-core locally; the Chromium binary lives in the
# user cache, not here. Both are reproducible from dev/browser-pass/package.json.
dev/browser-pass/node_modules/
dev/browser-pass/package-lock.json

# Real client water models Tom drops in to stress-test the .inp importer (ROADMAP Task 196). They
# carry client names and Windows Dropbox paths and this repo is on GitHub, so they stay local.
# dev/scripts/epanet_net_to_inp.php converts the .net ones; dev/lpn-spike/validate_inp.js reads
# whatever is here. Reverse this if Tom decides a model is his to publish.
#
# **THE DIRECTORY WAS RENAMED TO dev/water-network-examples/ ON 2026-08-14, AND A PATH-NAMED RULE
# DOES NOT FOLLOW A RENAME.** For a few minutes every client model in it was an ordinary untracked
# file one `git add <dir>` away from GitHub, with nothing to warn anybody -- the rename looked like
# a rename. The replacement lives in dev/water-network-examples/.gitignore and is a WHITELIST, so
# it cannot fail that way again: an unrecognised file there is ignored by default, and publishing
# one is an explicit line somebody has to write.
#
# This line is kept anyway, as a net under the old name, in case a model is ever dropped back into
# the path it lived in for the first half of August.
dev/epanet-models/

# Root npm is ACQUISITION ONLY -- there is no build and the site never reads node_modules.
# package-lock.json IS committed, deliberately, and is the whole point: `npm ci` reproducing the
# exact upstream tarball is what lets a future upgrade be VERIFIED rather than trusted. That is
# also why the root lockfile is tracked where dev/browser-pass/'s is not -- that one installs a
# tool, this one records what ships to visitors. See dev/dependency-management.md.
/node_modules/

# The Mapbox public token (ROADMAP Task 452). Not a secret, but not ours to publish either:
# the repo is public and the token is billable to Tom's account. lib/config.inc.php explains,
# and an absent file simply hides the satellite basemap. Uploaded to production by hand.
lib/mapbox-token.php
